{"id":"NCT02735707","title":"Randomized, Embedded, Multifactorial Adaptive Platform Trial for Community- Acquired Pneumonia","official":"Randomized, Embedded, Multifactorial Adaptive Platform Trial for Community- Acquired Pneumonia","summary":"REMAP-CAP is a randomised, embedded, multifactorial, adaptive platform trial for community-acquired pneumonia.\n\nThe purpose of this study is to evaluate the effect of a range of interventions to improve outcome of hospitalised patients admitted to intensive care with respiratory tract infections.\n\nIn addition, REMAP-CAP provides and adaptive research platform for evaluation of multiple treatment modalities in the event of a respiratory pandemic such as COVID-19.\n\nREMAP-COVID is a sub-platform of REMAP-CAP that evaluates treatments specific to COVID-19 in the United States of America.","conditions":["Respiratory Tract Diseases","Influenza (Pandemic)","Influenza","Community Acquired Pneumonia","Community Acquired Pneumonia (CAP)","Community Acquired Pneumonia, Severe","COVID-19","Respiratory Tract Infection Acute","Respiratory Tract Infections (RTI)","SARS CoV 2 Infection"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ceftriaxone + Macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Moxifloxacin or Levofloxacin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Piperacillin-tazobactam + Macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ceftaroline + Macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Amoxicillin-clavulanate + Macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Standard course macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Extended course macrolide"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No systemic corticosteroid"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Fixed-duration Hydrocortisone"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Shock-dependent hydrocortisone"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Fixed-duration higher dose Hydrocortisone"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No antiviral agent for influenza"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Five-days oseltamivir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ten-days oseltamivir"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No antiviral agent for COVID-19"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Lopinavir / Ritonavir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Hydroxychloroquine"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Hydroxychloroquine + lopinavir/ritonavir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ivermectin"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No immune modulation for COVID-19"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Interferon beta-1a"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Anakinra"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Tocilizumab"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Sarilumab"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Local standard venous thromboprophylaxis"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Therapeutic dose anticoagulation"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Conventional low dose thromboprophylaxis"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Intermediate dose thromboprophylaxis"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Continuation of therapeutic dose anticoagulation"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No immunoglobulin"},{"type":"BIOLOGICAL","name":"Convalescent plasma"},{"type":"BIOLOGICAL","name":"Delayed administration of convalescent plasma"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No vitamin C"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Vitamin C"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No antiplatelet"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Aspirin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"P2Y12 inhibitor"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No simvastatin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Simvastatin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Eritoran"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Apremilast"},{"type":"PROCEDURE","name":"Clinician-preferred mechanical ventilation strategy"},{"type":"PROCEDURE","name":"Protocolised mechanical ventilation strategy"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No renin-angiotensin system inhibitor"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Angiotensin converting enzyme inhibitor"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Angiotensin Receptor Blockers"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"ARB + DMX-200"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No cysteamine"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Cysteamine"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Fixed-duration dexamethasone"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Baloxavir Marboxil"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Five-days oseltamivir + baloxavir marboxil"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ten-days oseltamivir + baloxavir marboxil"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No endothelial modulator"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Imatinib"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No Immune Modulator for Influenza"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Tocilizumab"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Baricitinib"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"No antiviral agent for COVID-19"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Nirmatrelvir/ritonavir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Remdesivir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Nirmatrelvir/ritonavir + remdesivir"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Amoxicillin-clavulanate + Ceftazidime + Macrolide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Meropenem + Macrolide"}],"criteria":"The eligibility criteria for the Platform are applied at multiple levels. One level is that there are inclusion and exclusion criteria that determine eligibility for randomization within the Platform. Another level is that, once eligible for inclusion within the Platform, additional criteria (typically exclusion criteria) are applied that are specific to each domain. Finally, intervention-level eligibility criteria may be applied for interventions within a domain. A patient is eligible for inclusion within a domain when:\n\n* All Platform inclusion criteria are met\n* None of the Platform exclusion criteria are met\n* Domain-specific eligibility criteria are met\n* The patient is eligible for at least two interventions within a domain\n\nAs such, the key \"inclusion criteria\" for being eligible for a domain are that the patient is eligible for the Platform.\n\n\\--\n\nPLATFORM INCLUSION CRITERIA:\n\n1. Hospitalised patient\n2. Acute respiratory tract infection\n3. Aged 28 days or older\n\nPLATFORM EXCLUSION CRITERIA:\n\n1. Death is deemed to be imminent and inevitable during the next 24 hours AND one or more of the patient, substitute decision maker or attending physician are not committed to full active treatment\n2. Patient is expected to be discharged from hospital within the next 24 hours\n3. Previous participation in this REMAP within the last 90 days\n\nDOMAIN-SPECIFIC ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA:\n\nEach domain may have additional eligibility criteria. Refer to the study website for more information (www.remapcap.org).","minAge":"28 Days","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":20000,"start":"2016-04-11","pcd":"2028-06","upd":"2026-11-04","sponsor":"UMC Utrecht","areas":["other"],"central":["Cameron Green, MSc · info@remapcap.org","Svenja Peters, MSc · EU.remapcap@umcutrecht.nl"],"sites":[{"f":"CH Argenteuil","city":"Argenteuil","pr":"","zip":"95107","s":"ANR","lat":48.9479,"lon":2.2474,"c":""},{"f":"Centre Hospitalier Henri Mondor d'Aurillac","city":"Aurillac","pr":"","zip":"15000","s":"STOP","lat":44.9254,"lon":2.4398,"c":""},{"f":"Beauvais General Hospital","city":"Beauvais","pr":"","zip":"60000","s":"ANR","lat":49.4333,"lon":2.0833,"c":""},{"f":"Hopital Nord Franche-Comte","city":"Belfort","pr":"","zip":"90400","s":"SUS","lat":47.6422,"lon":6.8539,"c":""},{"f":"Centre hospitalier Bethune Beuvry","city":"Béthune","pr":"","zip":"62660","s":"R","lat":50.5296,"lon":2.64,"c":"Christophe Vinsonneau, MD"},{"f":"Ambroise Pare Hospital","city":"Boulogne-Billancourt","pr":"","zip":"92100","s":"R","lat":48.8355,"lon":2.2413,"c":"Antoine Vieillard Baron, MD"},{"f":"CH de Dax","city":"Dax","pr":"","zip":"40100","s":"R","lat":43.7103,"lon":-1.0537,"c":"Adrien Auvet, MD"},{"f":"Centre Hospitalier de Dieppe","city":"Dieppe","pr":"","zip":"76202","s":"R","lat":49.9216,"lon":1.0777,"c":"Peierre-Louis Declercq, MD"},{"f":"CHU Dijon Bourgogne","city":"Dijon","pr":"","zip":"21000","s":"R","lat":47.3134,"lon":5.0139,"c":"Jean-Pierre Quenot, MD"},{"f":"Hopital Simone Veil Eaubonne","city":"Eaubonne","pr":"","zip":"95600","s":"ANR","lat":48.9971,"lon":2.2825,"c":""},{"f":"Sud Essonne Hospital Etampes","city":"Étampes","pr":"","zip":"91150","s":"ANR","lat":48.4351,"lon":2.1623,"c":""},{"f":"Hospital Raymond Poincare","city":"Garches","pr":"","zip":"92380","s":"R","lat":48.8423,"lon":2.1823,"c":"Djillali Annane, MD"},{"f":"CHD Vendee","city":"La Roche-sur-Yon","pr":"","zip":"85000","s":"R","lat":46.6697,"lon":-1.4276,"c":"Gwenael Colin, MD